{
  "info": {
    "name": "Ory Kratos Mock API v1.3.1",
    "description": "Test collection for the mock Ory Kratos service. Base URL defaults to http://localhost:8119. In docker-compose, the service is reachable at http://ory-kratos-api:8119.\n\nKratos has no login endpoint. It has **self-service flows**, and they are first-class resources: create one with `GET /self-service/login/api`, then submit against its id with `POST /self-service/login?flow=<id>`. A failed submission is not an error body -- it is 400 with the whole flow re-rendered and messages attached to the offending `ui.nodes`, which is what a client draws. Numbered message ids carry the meaning: 4000001 required, 4000002 too short, 4000006 invalid credentials, 4000007 identifier exists, 4000038 not in enum.\n\nTraits are validated against the identity's JSON Schema. Two schemas are seeded with different required fields, so the same registration payload succeeds against `default` and fails against `partner`.\n\nSeeded flows can be quoted literally: login f1a0c7e2-5b93-4d68-8017-2e6f931c5d47 (api), d80c5f13-27ba-4e69-91d4-6a03e7b28c50 (browser, csrf csrf-a71e0c93d45b8f26), 2a97e0b8-4d16-43cf-8572-b1e0c9d64f35 (aal2 step-up), f6b23c91-08de-4a75-b3c0-97e15d24a608 (expired). Session tokens: ory_st_amelia_4c19f7e0b83d (aal2), ory_st_jonas_91e5c7d40a26, ory_st_helena_d502a8f371c6 (oidc), ory_st_priya_1d75a0e934bc, ory_st_amelia_revoked_3a6d80e5 (revoked). Requests labelled '(N expected)' assert an error path.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
